<title>GERMANY: Veba unit says chairman in investigative custody.</title>
<headline>Veba unit says chairman in investigative custody.</headline>
<dateline>DUESSELDORF, Germany</dateline>
<text>
<p>Veba Immobilien AG said Friday that Chairman Ulrich Lilienthal was in investigative custody on suspicion of using company funds to pay for private construction contracts.</p>
<p>Veba said its supervisory board would take up the matter Monday and make the necessary decisions on personnel matters.</p>
<p>The investigation was first announced Wednesday, but Lilienthal's alleged involvement was not mentioned.</p>
